    "kind": "ai-tool-descriptor",
    "id": "tool:read-business",
    "status": "active",
    "maker": "maker:see-what-my-business-took-in-this-month",
    "licence_class": "licence:maker-own",
    "label": "Read this account's business this month",
    "job": "Read what this account's business took in this month on the payment services it connected",
    "description": "The one read of the Business screen (tool:business). Returns since_words (the first of this month), service_names (the payment services whose money can be read), connected ([{label, state: read | none | unread, currencies: [{currency, code, multi, service_label, money_in, fees, refunded, net}] written in each currency, payments, more, at_most}], one per payment service, each read with the person's own account of it by running its money read, tool:stripe-events-read_money_since; a read that fails is unread, with no number) and operator (null: the operator's part has no owner here). Which services this account connected is read by running tool:list-connections with the connection_records and held_connections it is handed: a service it did not connect is not read and is drawn as not connected; when either list is not handed in or the listing cannot be read, the account of each service is asked of tool:find-the-account-of-a-service from the held_connections it is handed (one held: that one; several: refused, naming them; none: said as could not be read); with no held_connections each service is read with the service named and no account (service_connection:<service>), which only a key the vault holds under that bare id answers, so hand in held_connections (the vault's names, never a value). A person who holds more than one account of a service is refused, with the accounts named. Reads only.",
    "input_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "additionalProperties": false,
     "properties": {
      "now": {
       "type": "string",
       "description": "The time whose month is read (ISO); now when left out"
      },
      "connection_records": {
       "type": "array",
       "description": "The person's connection records as read from their store, [{ id, value }] (records of type connection); handed on to tool:list-connections, which reads no record itself. Without them (or without held_connections) the connections are unknown: each service's money is read with the service named and no account, for the engine to find the account the vault holds, and a failed read says it could not be read.",
       "items": {
        "type": "object"
       }
      },
      "held_connections": {
       "type": "array",
       "description": "The connections the account's vault holds, [{ connection_id, fields }], read from the vault's names, never a value; handed on to tool:list-connections with connection_records. Left out, it is never taken as no connections: the connections are unknown, as above.",
       "items": {
        "type": "object"
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "output_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "required": [
      "since_words",
      "service_names",
      "connected"
     ],
     "properties": {
      "since_words": {
       "type": "string"
      },
      "service_names": {
       "type": "array"
      },
      "connected": {
       "type": "array"
      }
     }
    },
